cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use ClimateNetAI in your research, please cite this software."

title: "ClimateNetAI: Reliability-Aware Climate-Adaptive 5G Intelligence"
version: 2.3.0
date-released: "2026-10-06"
type: software
license: MIT

authors:
  - family-names: "Michael"
    given-names: "Olohimai Juliet"

repository-code: "https://github.com/olohi184/ClimateNetAI"
url: "https://climatenetai.streamlit.app"

abstract: >
  ClimateNetAI is a climate-aware and reliability-aware machine-learning
  research platform for 5G signal-strength prediction under atmospheric
  variability. Version 2.3 extends the RAC-5G
  (Reliability-Aware Climate-Adaptive 5G) framework with a Reliability
  Boundary Engine (RBE), a telemetry-aware selective-prediction mechanism
  that assigns prospective TRUST, CAUTION, or ABSTAIN states using only
  completed prior telemetry. The frozen RBE research configuration uses
  a five-observation monitoring window, an 8.71 dB robust error threshold,
  a 0.80 operational coverage floor, and a 10.11 dB conformal half-width.
  The current prediction outcome is excluded from its own reliability-state
  assignment to prevent outcome leakage. RBE complements, rather than
  replaces, the existing RAC-5G model-health, degradation-detection,
  controlled-adaptation, and recovery-verification workflow. Version 2.3
  includes automated RBE unit tests and Streamlit application smoke testing.
  TRUST denotes an empirically supported operating state under the validated
  criteria and is not a guarantee of prediction correctness.

keywords:
  - machine learning
  - 5G
  - wireless communications
  - RSSI
  - climate-aware AI
  - reliability-aware machine learning
  - selective prediction
  - uncertainty quantification
  - atmospheric variability
  - adaptive systems
  - climate-resilient digital infrastructure
